        "collapsible_tab_UWQ8gk": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Overview",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Overview",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<p>The Mowrator S1 21″ 4WD 18Ah Wide Wheels Edition is built for steep, soft, and uneven terrain where additional tire footprint improves traction and stability.<br/><br/>🛤️ Up to 85% grade (40°) slope capability, ahead of the standard 4WD's 75% (37°).<br/>🏎️ Wide wheels increase footprint and distribute weight, reducing turf damage.<br/>🔋 56V 18Ah LiFePO4 battery, up to 2.25 hours runtime.<br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_Uf69Wz": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Product Information",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Product Information",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<h2>More Footprint, More Traction</h2><p>Standard wheels balance traction and turf protection well, but on soft, uneven, or steeper ground they can lose grip. The Wide Wheels Edition swaps in a wider tire footprint that spreads the mower's weight over more surface area, preventing wheel spin and slippage while actually reducing turf compaction compared to a narrower tire under the same load.</p><h2>85% Grade, Up From 75%</h2><p>The wider footprint and improved grip push the slope rating from the standard 4WD's 75% (37°) to 85% (40°), handling steeper terrain than the base configuration without the more aggressive Grip Tread tire needed for the 100% (45°) Grip Tread Tire Edition.</p><h2>Same Reliable S1 Platform</h2><p>21-inch cutting deck, adjustable cutting height from 1.5 to 4.3 inches, and a 56V 18Ah LiFePO4 battery delivering up to 2.25 hours of runtime and 1.125 acres per charge, depending on conditions.</p><h2>Warranty</h2><p>2 year warranty covering the main machine, remote, and battery.</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_X7L37G": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Warranty & Support",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Warranty & Support",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<p>Every Mowrator S1 4WD Wide Wheels Edition is backed by Mowrator's standard 2 year warranty, covering the main machine, the remote control, and the battery.</p><p><strong>What's covered</strong><br/><br/>Manufacturing defects and functional failures under normal residential use. Warranty service is handled through Mowrator's authorized repair network; you'll need proof of purchase (order date, model, and serial number) to file a claim.</p><p><strong>30 Day Money-Back Guarantee</strong><br/><br/>If the Wide Wheels Edition doesn't work out for your terrain, return it within 30 days of delivery for a refund.</p><p><strong>Our role</strong><br/><br/>As your dealer, we're your first point of contact. Reach out to us for setup help, order questions, or to get a warranty claim started, and we'll coordinate directly with Mowrator on your behalf.</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_HjeTwa": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Setup & Installation",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Setup & Installation",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<p>Getting the Wide Wheels Edition running takes about 15 to 20 minutes, most of it charging.</p><p><strong>In the box</strong><br/><br/>Mower body with 21 inch cutting deck, 18Ah battery, 600W charger, wide wheels (installed), Professional Remote Controller, tool bag, manual grass bag, mulching insert, and data cable.</p><p><strong>1. Charge the battery</strong><br/><br/>Before first use, fully charge the battery using the included charger.</p><p><strong>2. Assemble the grass bag</strong><br/><br/>Slide the fabric onto the metal frame, then fasten the rubber strips around the bag opening to the frame.</p><p><strong>3. Choose your clipping mode</strong><br/><br/>Mulch, rear bag, or side discharge, whichever fits the job.</p><p><strong>4. Seat the battery and pair the remote</strong><br/><br/>Power on the mower and the remote connects wirelessly. Indicator lights confirm connection status.</p><p><strong>5. Set your cutting height and walk the terrain first</strong><br/><br/>Especially on the steeper or uneven ground this edition is built for, walk the area first to clear debris before running a full pass.</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_czbJiW": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Specifications",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Specifications",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<p>Model: Mowrator S1 21″ 4WD 18Ah Wide Wheels Edition<br/><br/>Drive: Four-wheel drive (4WD)<br/><br/>Wheels: Wide wheels, PU material, increased footprint<br/><br/>Cutting width: 21 in<br/><br/>Cutting height range: 1.5 to 4.3 in, adjustable<br/><br/>Max slope rating: 85% grade (40°)<br/><br/>Battery: 56V LiFePO4, 18Ah<br/><br/>Runtime: up to 2.25 hours<br/><br/>Coverage per charge: up to 1.125 acres, depending on conditions<br/><br/>Clipping system: mulch, rear bag, or side discharge<br/><br/>Control method: handheld remote control<br/><br/>Warranty: 2 years on main machine, remote control, and battery<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
